      "explanation": "The highlighted red structure is the ischial spine and the pudendal nerve is related to it.\n\nThe pudendal nerve arises from S2-S4, exits the pelvis through the greater sciatic foramen, and enters the perineum by passing around the ischial spine. The ischial spine is used as a landmark for pudendal nerve block."
